            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0935" n="815" xml:id="pg815"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/871: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-14T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:04 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>494. On the resumption of Boxer indemnity payments this month I advise retained
                    portion be handled as it was before December 1917 when payments were deferred.
                    Same course might be followed with remitted portion also but I consider present
                    method of handling remitted portion preferable in view of guarantees it affords.
                    Please instruct by telegraph so I may notify Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
